<report>
<title>Sample size for independent case-control study</title>

<p>Probability of exposure in controls = <inu>pc</inu><br />
Probability of exposure in cases = <inu>ps</inu><br />
Controls per case subject = <in>cpc</in><br />
Alpha = <inu>alpha</inu><br />
Power = <inu>power</inu></p>

<p>For uncorrected chi-square test:<br />
N = <in>case</in> case subjects and <in>controls</in> controls</p>

<p><b>For corrected chi-square and Fisher's exact tests:</b><br />
N = <in>case_corr</in> case subjects and <in>controls_corr</in> controls</p>
<block name="assumptions">

<p><warn>NB:Assumptions of this calculation may cause over estimation of sample size when power is low.</warn><br />
<warn>However, true power associated with <in>cases</in> cases will be no less than <in>no_less</in> and no greater than <in>no_greater</in>.</warn></p>
</block>
</report>
